  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "2002 (May - Jun): Ichthyoplankton Survey Data in the Region Between Unimak Pass, the Shumagin Islands, and Through Shelikof Strait to Kodiak Island - R/V Miller Freeman (Cruise ID: MF2002-07)",
  "description": "The Alaska Fisheries Science Center FOCI program conducted an ichthyoplankton survey from Unimak Pass through Shelikof Strait and Kennedy Entrance. Data collected include ichthyoplankton, seawater temperature, seawater salinity, chlorophyll, nutrients, and microzooplankton. Cruise ID: MF2002-07 (23 May - 1 June 2002) Survey vessels: R/V Oshoro Maru For preliminary survey results see http://www.pmel.noaa.gov/foci/operations/instructions/2002/mf02-07/l1f.pdf\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To conduct an ichthyoplankton survey and process oriented studies in the region between Unimak Pass, the Shumagin Islands, and through Shelikof Strait to Kodiak Island, Alaska, to estimate the abundance of young walleye pollock larvae, their transport, and factors influencing their survival.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23569822",
